The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (!zero_memory) {
    // Memory allocation without zeroing
}
```
```c
struct page *page = get_page(pfn);
```
```c
// Attempt to write directly into page tables
xen_set_pud(...);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the change in behavior from commit f7f99100d8d9 stopped zeroing memory during allocation in `vmemmap`, which caused the "Pinned" information in the `struct page` of early page tables to be lost for Xen PV domains. As a result, when the kernel tried to access the page tables, it attempted to write directly into them instead of delegating this operation to the hypervisor, leading to a kernel crash due to an invalid memory access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (xen_pv_domain())
    return true;
```
```c
// Ensure early initialization of page structures for Xen PV domains
```
Reason:
The fix involves checking if the system is running as a Xen PV domain and ensuring that the page structures are initialized early. This prevents the loss of the "Pinned" information in the `struct page`, allowing the kernel to correctly interact with the hypervisor for page table management, thus avoiding the crash.

